SUMMARY:Jazz performance - FLUX Quartet
DESCRIPTION:An afternoon of adventurous contemporary music from "one of the 
 most fearless and important new-music ensembles around." (San Francisco 
 Chronicle) FLUX Quartet will perform compositions by legendary jazz 
 saxophonist and longtime Montclair resident Oliver Lake\, including a new 
 work for string quartet\, in addition to works by other 
 composers.\n\n\n\nFor nearly three decades\, FLUX has been a leading 
 interpreter of contemporary classical and creative music\, from Morton 
 Feldman\, Gyorgy Ligeti and Conlon Nancarrow to jazz avant-gardists Ornette 
 Coleman\, Henry Threadgill\, and John Zorn. They have performed at major 
 concert venues\, including Carnegie's Zankel Hall and the Kennedy Center\, 
 and served as artist-in-residence at major universities\, including 
 Princeton\, Dartmouth\, and Wesleyan. Music critic Alex Ross described 
 their live performance as "\n\n"a disorienting\, transfixing experience 
 that repeatedly approached and touched the sublime." (The New Yorker) FLUX 
 is Tom Chiu (violin)\, Conrad Harris (violin)\, Josh Henderson (viola)\, 
 and Rubin Kodheli (cello).\n\n\n\n\nOliver Lake is best known as a 
 trailblazing avant-garde alto saxophonist\, composer and bandleader. He 
 co-founded the pioneering World Saxophone Quartet and Trio 3 (with Reggie 
 Workman and Andrew Cyrille)\, founded The Oliver Lake Big Band\, Jump Up\, 
 and The Oliver Lake Organ Quartet\, and composed commissioned works for the 
 Brooklyn Philharmonic and Pro Musica Chamber Orchestra. His many 
 collaborations include not just fellow jazz greats but Bjork\, Lou Reed\, A 
 Tribe Called Quest\, Mos Def\, and Me’shell Ndegeocello. Lake is a 
 recipient of the Doris Duke Artist Award\, a Guggenheim Fellowship\, and 
 the Mellon Jazz Living Legacy Award. He  is also an accomplished poet\, 
 visual artist\, and performance artist. An exhibition of select visual 
 works\, EN SOULS\, will be on display at the library Sept 1-29.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-16269242
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16269242
