SUMMARY:Charcoal Drawing for Non-Artists NEW
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Montclair Public Library for an afternoon that 
 will change the way you think about drawing. Working from fresh flowers\, 
 fruit\, and carefully curated objects\, participants will learn the 
 timeless techniques artists use to create realistic tonal drawings with 
 charcoal. This workshop regularly leaves participants surprised by 
 what\nthey are capable of creating in just one session.\n\nMore than a 
 drawing class\, it's an introduction to the art of looking—a skill that 
 can be practiced and enjoyed for years to come. If you're not easily 
 impressed by your artistic abilities\, prepare to surprise yourself. All 
 skills levels and self-proclaimed "non-artists" are welcome. A little 
 charcoal dust is part of the experience\, so wearing an old shirt is 
 recommended.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
