DTEND:20260917T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260917T000000Z
SUMMARY:Why Are We Involved in Cuba? Unravelling Tensions Between D.C. and Havana NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nThe troubled relationship between Cuba and the United States 
 is like no other. Only 90 miles of water separate the two nations\, but 
 they have remained far apart politically\, economically\, and ideologically 
 for more than 60 years.\n\nIn this class\, we will explore the roots of the 
 enmity between Cuba and the U.S.\, tracing the evolving landscape from the 
 the initial rumblings of the Cuban Revolution in the 1950s\, through the 
 rise of Fidel Castro\, the hardening of U.S. positions on Cuba's 
 leadership\, through the current confrontation as Washington clamps down on 
 Cuba's economy. How did we get here? Why are we here? And where is all this 
 going?
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
