SUMMARY:Chinese Brush Painting for the Moon Festival NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nJoin our celebration of the Chinese Mid-Autumn Moon Festival! 
 The instructor will begin this class with a 45-minute talk about the 
 holiday while she simultaneously creates a brush painting of Chang'e\, the 
 Moon Goddess who drank an immortality potion and floated up to live in the 
 sky. After a 15-minute break\, students will have 90 minutes for a hands-on 
 workshop on brush-painting chrysanthemums\, a classic symbol of fall in 
 China. The Folklife Center of Northern NJ will also provide traditional 
 mooncake cookies and chrysanthemum tea for participants to 
 sample.\n\nCo-sponsored by the Folklife Center of Northern NJ.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Classroom\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts, Lectures / History & Culture
