SUMMARY:Excel 1
DESCRIPTION:\n\nThis is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nThe class is geared to beginners and those who seek a 
 refresher in the topic.  Students will gain a basic understanding of the 
 worksheet environment\, tools for working with data\, and resources for 
 continued learning.\n\nThis is a hands-on class\; students should be able 
 to use the mouse and keyboard. Students are welcome to bring a flash drive 
 to save their work for review and practice.\n\nSummary of Topics:\n\nClass 
 1:  Worksheet basics using a budget - Learn elements of the worksheet\, 
 enter and edit budget data\, perform calculations\, create a pie 
 chart.\n\nClass 2:  Format a worksheet for an attractive\, easily-readable 
 on-screen presentation as well with the attributes needed for 
 printing.\n\nClass 3: Formulas & Functions – learn more about how to use 
 formulas\, and the wide array of built-in functions.  Includes the concepts 
 of relative and absolute cell references\, named ranges in formulas\; and 
 how to create and use a Table to streamline your work.  [After this class\, 
 students will be ready to work with Pivot Tables\, an even more powerful 
 way to work with data.]\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Computers & Technology
UID:LibCal-10306-17224995
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17224995
