SUMMARY:Tasting History: Bagel-Making Workshop NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nTASTING HISTORY is a two-hour\, hands-on workshop in which 
 participants mix\, shape\, boil\, and bake old-school New York bagels\, 
 while learning about the bagel’s deep connection to the New York City 
 area’s history and community. This workshop combines making and 
 meaning.\n\nBy the end of class\, participants will come to see the bagel 
 as far more than a simple bread roll. We’ll explain that it tracks some 
 of the most fascinating and important developments in the story of the 
 lower east side\, of the city as a whole\, and of the country 
 itself.\n\n\nThe bagel’s appearance in America is a result of our 
 country’s early immigration policy...It played a role in the growth of 
 organized labor...And it’s also a prime example of the changes in the 
 American diet.\n\n\nIn short\, the TASTING HISTORY class blends kitchen 
 skills\, cultural storytelling\, and community engagement in
LOCATION:Montclair - Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Montclair\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Culinary
