SUMMARY:The Library of Alexandria NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nThe Library of Alexandria was the ancient world's boldest 
 experiment: an attempt to gather every book on earth under one roof. Its 
 story has become intertwined with famous figures like Cleopatra and Julius 
 Caesar\, making it difficult to separate fact from legend. Did it hold half 
 a million scrolls? Did it burn to the ground in a single night? This talk 
 explores who filled its shelves\, who studied there\, and what really 
 happened to it. We'll then visit the Bibliotheca Alexandrina\, the 
 impressive modern library that opened in 2002 near where the ancient one 
 once stood.\n\nPresented by Jenny Montasir\, Montclair State professor and 
 founder of EgyptEd.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-17115130
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17115130
