SUMMARY:Building Your Financial Roadmap: A Financial Wellness Series
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nTake control of your financial future with this four-part 
 financial wellness workshop series designed to help you build a stronger 
 foundation for making informed money decisions. Each workshop focuses on a 
 practical aspect of financial wellness\, from understanding how money grows 
 and creating a plan for where your money should go\, to preparing your 
 family and planning for retirement.\n\nWhether you're just getting 
 started\, looking to strengthen your financial habits\, or preparing for 
 the future\, you'll gain practical knowledge\, useful tools\, and 
 actionable strategies you can apply to your own financial life.\n\nEach 
 week we'll answer one important question about your financial 
 future:\n\n\n	\n	How does money grow?\n	\n\n\n\n	\n	Where should my money 
 go first?\n	\n\n\n\n	\n	How do I prepare my family for the 
 future?\n	\n\n\n\n	\n	How do I prepare myself for 
 retirement?\n	\n\n\nWhether you attend one workshop or the entire series\, 
 you'll leave with practical knowledge and actionable steps to help you make 
 informed financial decisions.\n\nThese workshops are for educational 
 purposes only and are intended to provide general financial education. They 
 should not be considered individualized financial\, legal\, tax\, or 
 investment advice.\n
LOCATION:Montclair Bellevue Ave Branch - First Floor\, Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Finances
UID:LibCal-10306-17190733
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17190733
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260930T223000Z
DTEND:20261001T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260930T000000Z
SUMMARY:Home Repair Essentials
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nLearn the fundamentals of home repair in this practical\, 
 hands-on workshop taught by Robert Haas\, instructor of the popular 
 Woodworking 101 and Advanced Woodworking classes. Held at Montclair High 
 School\, this course gives participants a behind-the-walls look at how 
 common home features are built and maintained.\n\nDuring the class\, 
 instructor Rob Haas will construct two demonstration walls that include 
 doors and a window\, showing how these elements are installed and how 
 typical wall structures are assembled. Participants will also learn how 
 traditional double-hung windows operate and how they can be repaired\, 
 including basic glass pane replacement.\n\nThe workshop will also introduce 
 the basics of residential wiring\, demonstrating how outlets and lighting 
 are installed and connected. Throughout the session\, Robert will answer 
 questions and offer guidance on a wide range of home repair 
 topics.\n\nWhether you're a homeowner looking to handle basic repairs 
 yourself or simply curious about how things in your home work\, this class 
 provides practical knowledge you can use right away.\n
LOCATION:Montclair - Montclair High School\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Arts & Crafts
