DTEND:20261008T181500Z
DTSTAMP:20261008T000000Z
SUMMARY:Everything Book Club\, "The Ministry of Time" by Kaliene Bradley\, Session 2
DESCRIPTION:An instant New York Times bestseller. In the near future\, a 
 new government ministry is exploring time travel. Our heroine gets a highly 
 paid job assisting and monitoring the time travel expat known as “1847” 
 or Commander Graham Gore. As far as history is concerned\, Commander Gore 
 died on a doomed 1845 expedition to the Arctic\, so he’s a little 
 disoriented by living with an unmarried woman who regularly shows her 
 calves\, uses outlandish devices such as “washing machines” and 
 “Spotify\,” and talks about “the collapse of the British Empire.”  
 This witty\, sexy\, genre-bending debut novel will tug your heartstrings\, 
 make you laugh\, and ultimately make you think.\n\n"A hilarious yet 
 poignant take on dislocation\, loss\, and oddball community . . .  A twisty 
 plotline that incorporates plenty of John le Carré and Mick Herron 
 spy-craft references . . .  with the silly\, incisive\, and spot-on comedy 
 of Douglas Adams."—The Boston Globe\n\nKaliane Bradley is a 
 British-Cambodian writer and editor based in London. Her short fiction has 
 appeared in Somesuch Stories\, The Willowherb Review\, Electric 
 Literature\, Catapult\, and Extra Teeth\, among others. She was the winner 
 of the 2022 Harper’s Bazaar Short Story Prize and the 2022 V.S. Pritchett 
 Short Story Prize.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-17560859
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17560859
