SUMMARY:Two Eyes Screening Event
DESCRIPTION:Newark LGBTQ Center\, Out Montclair and The Montclair Public 
 Library invite you to an exclusive screening of Two Eyes\, featuring 
 Academy Award nominee Lily Gladstone.\n\nIn 19th century Montana\, a 
 painter's worldview is challenged by his Native American guide while 
 exploring a new landscape. In 1970s California\, a teenager’s life is 
 shaken up by the arrival of an enigmatic transfer student. In present-day 
 Wyoming\, a trans youth attempts to work through his complex emotions with 
 a nonbinary therapist. Two Eyes weaves together three distinct tales of 
 queer identity into a single narrative exploring the power of human 
 connection.\n\nIN-PERSON SCREENING: Friday\, October 9th at 7:00 p.m. EDT 
 at the Montclair Library followed by a 45-minute live Zoom conversation 
 with filmmaker Travis Fine. There is a suggested cash-only donation of 
 $20.\n\nContent Warning(s): Racially or Sexually Motivated Violence. This 
 film does not have a formal rating\, but overall themes are mature.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-10306-17612209
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17612209
END:VEVENT
