SUMMARY:Cookbook Swap & Baked Goods Tasting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for another Cookbook Swap!\n\nCookbook Swap: 10:30 
 AM–1:30 PM | Café Area\nBaked Goods Tasting: 12:00–1:30 PM | 
 Auditorium\n\nBring your gently used cookbooks and exchange them 1-for-1 
 with fellow culinary enthusiasts. Maximum of 5 books.\n\n\n	\n	Drop off 
 your cookbooks at the library in advance\, prior to October 10.\n	\n	On the 
 day of the event\, for every cookbook you’ve donated\, you’ll get to 
 choose a new one to take home!\n\n\nAnd this time\, we’re adding 
 something delicious! You can bring a homemade baked good for fellow 
 cookbook lovers to sample and enjoy. Please bring your baked good ready to 
 serve—there will be no heating\, reheating\, or cooking of food at the 
 event. Bringing a baked good is completely optional—you’re welcome to 
 attend the cookbook swap and bake-off even if you don’t bring food.\n\nIf 
 you plan to bring a baked good\, please email 
 adultprograms@montclairlibrary.org and let us know what you will be 
 bringing. All baked goods must be nut-free.\n\nPlease note: Baked goods may 
 contain other common allergens\, and the library cannot guarantee an 
 allergen-free environment or be responsible for allergic reactions or other 
 food-related sensitivities. Please use your best judgment when sampling 
 foods.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater, Culinary
